{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfPk1LPXzjiaTnmZ6R9Sz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't do this one as asked, and I want to be direct about why before you're up against your deadline.\n\nWebSearch and WebFetch are both blocked in this session (permission not granted), so I have no way to verify a single citation. For a piece running as-is under your byline, me producing \"author, title, publication, year\" strings from memory is the worst possible failure mode — fabricated citations look exactly like real ones until your editor or a reader checks them. I'm not going to hand you a printable citation list I can't stand behind.\n\nHere's what I can honestly give you.\n\n## What I recall with reasonable confidence (verify before print)\n\n- **Date and place:** Sunday 13 July 1980, Hollinwell showground near Kirkby-in-Ashfield, Nottinghamshire.\n- **Event:** a juvenile jazz/marching band championship — hundreds of children in uniform, several thousand spectators, an early start on a hot, humid morning.\n- **Symptoms:** fainting, dizziness, nausea and vomiting, sore eyes and throat, limb weakness. Onset spread rapidly through the crowd over the morning.\n- **Explanations investigated at the time:** pesticide/organophosphate spray drift from adjacent farmland (a nearby field was reported to have been sprayed shortly beforehand); food poisoning from on-site vendors; contaminated water; heat, dehydration and prolonged standing; and mass psychogenic illness (\"mass hysteria\"), which became the leading official explanation.\n- **Contested outcome:** no toxic agent was ever identified. The psychogenic conclusion was widely rejected by the families involved, and that dispute is a large part of why the incident is still written about.\n\n## What I will not state, even loosely\n\n- **The casualty figure.** This is the number you specifically asked for, and it's the single most-likely-wrong thing I could tell you. Published accounts differ on whether the figure counts everyone affected, everyone treated on site, or only hospital admissions — I'd be guessing which convention any given number follows.\n- **Any citation.** I have vague associations with mass-sociogenic-illness literature by Simon Wessely and by Robert Bartholomew, and with the earlier Blackburn 1965 outbreak literature (a different incident, often cited alongside Hollinwell). Those are search leads for you, not citations. Do not print them on my say-so — including the years, which I'd be reconstructing.\n\n## Fastest routes to verified sourcing tonight\n\n1. **Contemporary press:** the Nottingham Evening Post and national papers, 14–20 July 1980. The British Newspaper Archive and the Times Digital Archive both have same-day coverage with the on-the-day figures.\n2. **Official record:** Hansard (hansard.parliament.uk) — the incident drew parliamentary questions; those contain the official casualty figures and name the investigating bodies.\n3. **Medical literature:** search PubMed for `Hollinwell`, and for `mass psychogenic illness` / `mass sociogenic illness` limited to 1980–1990. PubMed gives you exact author, title, journal, year, ready to print.\n4. **The official investigation report** itself, via Nottinghamshire Archives or the relevant health authority records.\n\nIf you can grant web access in this session, I'll run all four and build you the sourced fact sheet properly — that's maybe fifteen minutes of work, and it's the version you actually want. Alternatively, paste me the sources you've already gathered and I'll write and structure the piece around them.\n\nOne thing worth telling your editor either way: the casualty count and the \"mass hysteria\" framing are both genuinely contested in the sources rather than settled facts, so the piece will be stronger if it attributes each to whoever claimed it rather than asserting either flat."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":290,"cache_read_input_tokens":32450,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":290},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d57d8bf4-76bb-4716-98c5-b5cc25e43280","uuid":"87e6ad8d-2ed3-4891-807b-f5d27878e424","timestamp":"2026-09-25T07:12:59.798Z","request_id":"req_011CfPk1KxUzp7GANbgF2ivi"}
